{"title":"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The length of a rectangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92ecfc3cd18f0b81a25b50dd59ae837f7bb74cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />, is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de1a36d69a7028480a87b712a7141c651398a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> and its width is decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />. If the area of the resulting rectangle is equal to the area of the original rectangle, determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Variables.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Variables)\">Solution 1 (Variables)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Variables)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee61fd6e8a1926a802b97fc99b66b8687d8f620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> be the original length of the rectangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the original width of the rectangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d69232050ab0ada641e7e2035f6e7c795795b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"15\" /> be the new length of the rectangle. The area of the rectangle is then originally <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbee742ced1a3a451de168714734481409319148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1 \\times w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since the width of the rectangle is decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, the new width must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f4ac7fe4d2dce2b1ffa3c899790c9f44682db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{10}w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />. The area of the new rectangle is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97eedcbd578eec0bc12f370f7a65e3392cad4e66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2 \\times \\frac{8}{10}w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />. However, we know that this is also equal to the area of the old rectangle, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca41af9a78261b573b407b2a943226d91623fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2 \\times \\frac{8}{10}w = l_1 \\times w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a6a1f95ff6cfe0c0090f7d696e3c56a2a35d922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2 = l_1 \\times \\frac{10w}{8w} = \\frac{5}{4}l_1 = 1.25l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"229\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>From this, we can realize that the width would have had to increase by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32b43fc61f457e9448091427eaae6ebeec0ce154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_2 = 1.25l_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61748119449aece73356ff4e791b72344c0b8d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 66/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 79/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2935/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.949      1 2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    5.949      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36317:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018032314 and revision id 281336. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}